ate":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID174","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for yelling at my wife about eating nutella from the jar? T","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for yelling at my wife about eating nutella from the jar? Throwaway account.\n\nMy wife is seven months pregnant, and we are ecstatic to be welcoming this child into the world. That said, as most gentlemen with pregnant wives know, this time is hard for them. My wife has been craving nutella a lot for the past two weeks. She doesn&#x27;t want to be eating it in abundance, so she has a spoonful or so once every few days. She uses a new spoon for each bite, but I do not agree with this.\n\nI&#x27;ve told her that this is probably not good for the baby, and there is research that indicates it can cause gestational diabetes. We got into an argument about this, where she claims that I am policing her eating choices, but I think since she is carrying my child, I have the right to have opinions about what she eats. People might say this is a douchebag thing to say, but I think that this is a team project and she has to be more understanding.\n\nUltimately, the argument escalated, I yelled a little and she got upset with me and hasn&#x27;t spoken to me in two hours. Am I wrong for here?<\/div><\/div><p><strong>Do you think the writer was in the wrong?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"v_1902","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for yelling at my wife about eating nutella from the jar? T","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely not in the wrong"},"2":{"Display":"Probably not in the wrong"},"3":{"Display":"Unsure"},"4":{"Display":"Probably in the wrong"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely in the wrong"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID174","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID175","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_v_1902","QuestionID":"QID175","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID176","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for yelling at my wife about eating nutella from the jar? T","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for yelling at my wife about eating nutella from the jar? Throwaway account.\n\nMy wife is seven months pregnant, and we are ecstatic to be welcoming this child into the world. That said, as most gentlemen with pregnant wives know, this time is hard for them. My wife has been craving nutella a lot for the past two weeks. She doesn&#x27;t want to be eating it in abundance, so she has a spoonful or so once every few days. She uses a new spoon for each bite, but I do not agree with this.\n\nI&#x27;ve told her that this is probably not good for the baby, and there is research that indicates it can cause gestational diabetes. We got into an argument about this, where she claims that I am policing her eating choices, but I think since she is carrying my child, I have the right to have opinions about what she eats. People might say this is a douchebag thing to say, but I think that this is a team project and she has to be more understanding.\n\nUltimately, the argument escalated, I yelled a little and she got upset with me and hasn&#x27;t spoken to me in two hours. Am I wrong for here?<\/div><\/div><p><em>You can re-read the situation above while evaluating the responses.<\/em><\/p><p>Here are two responses to the writer.<\/p><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;align-items:start\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response A<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option A}<\/div><\/div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response B<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option B}<\/div><\/div><\/div><p><strong>Overall, how good is each response?<\/strong><\/p><p>Rate each response:<\/p><p><strong>Response A<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gA_1902","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for yelling at my wife about eating nutella from the jar? T","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID176","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID177","SecondaryAttribute":"Response B","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Response B<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gB_1902","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Response B","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID177","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID178","SecondaryAttribute":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"l_1902","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely Response A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably Response A"},"3":{"Display":"About equally likely to listen to both"},"4":{"Display":"Probably Response B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely Response B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID178","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID179","SecondaryAttribute":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would you rather get advice from?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"a_1902","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely commenter A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably commenter A"},"3":{"Display":"No preference"},"4":{"Display":"Probably commenter B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely commenter B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID179","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID18","SecondaryAttribute":"Harvard University Area IRB protocol IRB25-1330. Principal Investigator: Dr.\u00a0Julia Minson. Versio..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"max-width:720px;line-height:1.45\">\n<p style=\"font-size:0.9em;color:#555\"><em>Harvard University Area IRB protocol IRB25-1330. Principal Investigator: Dr.&nbsp;Julia Minson. Version date: 2026.08.13.<\/em><\/p>\n\n<h2>Consent to Participate in Research<\/h2>\n<p><strong>Study:<\/strong> Evaluating Advice Responses to Interpersonal Disagreements<br>\n<strong>PI:<\/strong> Dr. Julia Minson (Harvard Kennedy School)<\/p><p><br><\/p>\n\n<p>You are invited to take part in a research study on how people evaluate advice about interpersonal disagreements. Participation is voluntary. You may skip questions or stop at any time without penalty.<\/p><p><br><\/p>\n\n<p><strong>What you will do.<\/strong> This online survey takes about <strong>8\u201312 minutes<\/strong>. You will read 5 short situations (lightly edited posts from a public advice forum), say whether you think the writer was in the wrong, read two unlabeled advice responses, and rate those responses.&nbsp;<\/p><p><br><\/p>\n\n<p><strong>Risks &amp; benefits.<\/strong> Risks are minimal (possible mild discomfort reading about conflict or critical advice; small confidentiality risk, minimized by secure storage and de-identified analysis). There are no guaranteed direct benefits; your responses may help research on advice and constructive communication.<\/p><p><br><\/p>\n\n<p><strong>Payment.<\/strong> You will be paid <strong>$2.50<\/strong>&nbsp;for completing the survey in full (about 8\u201312 minutes). If you do not consent, fail required attention checks, or return the Prolific submission without completing, you may not receive full payment (per platform rules).<\/p><p><br><\/p>\n\n<p><strong>Privacy.<\/strong> Data are analyzed in de-identified form. Prolific IDs may be used only for payment and data-quality review and will not be shared in public deposits. De-identified data may be shared for research transparency (e.g., OSF). Data will not be used to train AI models. The survey platform may record interaction timing for research and data quality.<\/p><p><br><\/p>\n\n<p><strong>Questions or concerns.<\/strong> Contact Dr. Julia Minson at <a href=\"mailto:julia_minson@hks.harvard.edu\">julia_minson@hks.harvard.edu<\/a> or (617) 495-3204. For questions about your rights as a research participant, contact the Harvard University Area IRB at (617) 496-2847 or <a href=\"mailto:cuhs@harvard.edu\">cuhs@harvard.edu<\/a>.<\/p><p><br><\/p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement of consent.<\/strong> Being in this study is completely voluntary. Please indicate whether you consent to participate and to having your de-identified data included in analyses for research purposes. Please save or print a copy of this page for your records.<\/p>\n<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"consent","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Harvard University Area IRB protocol IRB25-1330. Principal Investigator: Dr.\u00a0Julia Minson. Versio...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"I consent to participate"},"2":{"Display":"I do not consent"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID18","PrivateData":false,"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"NextChoiceId":3,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID180","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_r_1902","QuestionID":"QID180","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID181","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for being angry at wife because she tries to \"manage\" my sa","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for being angry at wife because she tries to &quot;manage&quot; my salary Me and my wife(no kids) don&#x27;t have a common budget.\nBecause I&#x27;m earning almost 4 times more than her, I willingly handle most of our expenses (around 80-90% of our expenses). She can use her own salary for whatever she wants(she&#x27;s saving around 40-60% of it).\n\nI have been helping my other family (parents &amp; brothers) with a mortgage for some years, but also with additional money when they needed. Still, I could save some and live a cozy life with my wife.\n\nLast time I helped them with a sum of around 25% of my monthly salary, my wife was angry at me. Her main argument is that I&#x27;m not saving for &quot;us&quot; (we&#x27;re planning to buy our own flat) and that she doesn&#x27;t have a say on our finances.\n\nI got really angry because this was not her first time and told her that you&#x27;ll never be able to manage the money I earn with this attitude of selfishness towards my other family. Also, I told her that even If I decide to donate half of my salary, she should support my decision as long as I&#x27;m covering both of us.<\/div><\/div><p><strong>Do you think the writer was in the wrong?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"v_2769","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for being angry at wife because she tries to \"manage\" my sa","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely not in the wrong"},"2":{"Display":"Probably not in the wrong"},"3":{"Display":"Unsure"},"4":{"Display":"Probably in the wrong"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely in the wrong"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID181","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID182","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_v_2769","QuestionID":"QID182","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID183","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for being angry at wife because she tries to \"manage\" my sa","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for being angry at wife because she tries to &quot;manage&quot; my salary Me and my wife(no kids) don&#x27;t have a common budget.\nBecause I&#x27;m earning almost 4 times more than her, I willingly handle most of our expenses (around 80-90% of our expenses). She can use her own salary for whatever she wants(she&#x27;s saving around 40-60% of it).\n\nI have been helping my other family (parents &amp; brothers) with a mortgage for some years, but also with additional money when they needed. Still, I could save some and live a cozy life with my wife.\n\nLast time I helped them with a sum of around 25% of my monthly salary, my wife was angry at me. Her main argument is that I&#x27;m not saving for &quot;us&quot; (we&#x27;re planning to buy our own flat) and that she doesn&#x27;t have a say on our finances.\n\nI got really angry because this was not her first time and told her that you&#x27;ll never be able to manage the money I earn with this attitude of selfishness towards my other family. Also, I told her that even If I decide to donate half of my salary, she should support my decision as long as I&#x27;m covering both of us.<\/div><\/div><p><em>You can re-read the situation above while evaluating the responses.<\/em><\/p><p>Here are two responses to the writer.<\/p><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;align-items:start\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response A<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option A}<\/div><\/div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response B<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option B}<\/div><\/div><\/div><p><strong>Overall, how good is each response?<\/strong><\/p><p>Rate each response:<\/p><p><strong>Response A<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gA_2769","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for being angry at wife because she tries to \"manage\" my sa","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID183","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID184","SecondaryAttribute":"Response B","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Response B<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gB_2769","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Response B","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID184","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID185","SecondaryAttribute":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"l_2769","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely Response A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably Response A"},"3":{"Display":"About equally likely to listen to both"},"4":{"Display":"Probably Response B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely Response B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID185","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID186","SecondaryAttribute":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would you rather get advice from?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"a_2769","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely commenter A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably commenter A"},"3":{"Display":"No preference"},"4":{"Display":"Probably commenter B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely commenter B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID186","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID187","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_r_2769","QuestionID":"QID187","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID188","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for telling my wife she probably shouldn't go to med school","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for telling my wife she probably shouldn&#x27;t go to med school? I&#x27;m (36) and in my last year of law school. Throughout the process, my wife (33) has been super supportive, and a fantastic mother to our 2 year old. Now that I&#x27;m poised to graduate, she rightfully wants to pursue her career. She&#x27;s determined to be a dermatologist. However, I voiced some concerns. Namely, the HUGE time commitment that med school will be. She seems to brush it off, much to my frustration. She has yet to start undergraduate school, so that&#x27;s 4 years. From what I understand, med school will be an additional 4 years, and another 3-7 years of residency. Even under the most liberal estimation, that&#x27;s another 11 years before she&#x27;s an MD. Not to mention that during that time she will basically be MIA due to the demand of med school. Meanwhile, I will be taking the bar and starting an extremely demanding career where I will be the sole money maker and caretaker of our 2 year old.\n\nI&#x27;ve never said she should NOT go, only that the time commitment is very real, and that she should consider alternatives such as Nurse Practitioner, OT school, etc. Yet, every time the conversation has come up she gets SUPER defensive. She&#x27;s even said, &quot;maybe we should just get a divorce and I can do what I want.&quot;\n\nI want to be supportive, and honestly, if she already had undergrad under he belt (as I did before starting law school) I&#x27;d be more behind the idea.\n\nSo, Am I wrong for telling my wife that she probably shouldn&#x27;t go to med school?<\/div><\/div><p><strong>Do you think the writer was in the wrong?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"v_2630","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for telling my wife she probably shouldn't go to med school","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely not in the wrong"},"2":{"Display":"Probably not in the wrong"},"3":{"Display":"Unsure"},"4":{"Display":"Probably in the wrong"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely in the wrong"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID188","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID189","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_v_2630","QuestionID":"QID189","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID19","SecondaryAttribute":"Almost done Think of one of the situations you just read and one of the response","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<h2>Almost done<\/h2><p>Think of one of the situations you just read and one of the responses you saw. In your own words, quote or paraphrase that response (at least a short sentence):<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"outro_paraphrase","QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"SL","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Almost done Think of one of the situations you just read and one of the response","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID19","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID190","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for telling my wife she probably shouldn't go to med school","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for telling my wife she probably shouldn&#x27;t go to med school? I&#x27;m (36) and in my last year of law school. Throughout the process, my wife (33) has been super supportive, and a fantastic mother to our 2 year old. Now that I&#x27;m poised to graduate, she rightfully wants to pursue her career. She&#x27;s determined to be a dermatologist. However, I voiced some concerns. Namely, the HUGE time commitment that med school will be. She seems to brush it off, much to my frustration. She has yet to start undergraduate school, so that&#x27;s 4 years. From what I understand, med school will be an additional 4 years, and another 3-7 years of residency. Even under the most liberal estimation, that&#x27;s another 11 years before she&#x27;s an MD. Not to mention that during that time she will basically be MIA due to the demand of med school. Meanwhile, I will be taking the bar and starting an extremely demanding career where I will be the sole money maker and caretaker of our 2 year old.\n\nI&#x27;ve never said she should NOT go, only that the time commitment is very real, and that she should consider alternatives such as Nurse Practitioner, OT school, etc. Yet, every time the conversation has come up she gets SUPER defensive. She&#x27;s even said, &quot;maybe we should just get a divorce and I can do what I want.&quot;\n\nI want to be supportive, and honestly, if she already had undergrad under he belt (as I did before starting law school) I&#x27;d be more behind the idea.\n\nSo, Am I wrong for telling my wife that she probably shouldn&#x27;t go to med school?<\/div><\/div><p><em>You can re-read the situation above while evaluating the responses.<\/em><\/p><p>Here are two responses to the writer.<\/p><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;align-items:start\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response A<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option A}<\/div><\/div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response B<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option B}<\/div><\/div><\/div><p><strong>Overall, how good is each response?<\/strong><\/p><p>Rate each response:<\/p><p><strong>Response A<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gA_2630","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for telling my wife she probably shouldn't go to med school","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID190","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID191","SecondaryAttribute":"Response B","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Response B<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gB_2630","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Response B","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID191","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID192","SecondaryAttribute":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"l_2630","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely Response A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably Response A"},"3":{"Display":"About equally likely to listen to both"},"4":{"Display":"Probably Response B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely Response B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID192","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID193","SecondaryAttribute":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would you rather get advice from?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"a_2630","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely commenter A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably commenter A"},"3":{"Display":"No preference"},"4":{"Display":"Probably commenter B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely commenter B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID193","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID194","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_r_2630","QuestionID":"QID194","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID195","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for barring entry to my party with a quiz? I am hosting a R","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for barring entry to my party with a quiz? I am hosting a Rick and Morty screening party in my dorm room next week. I am one of the only people in the dorm with a good TV so a lot of people want to come but the room can&#x27;t accommodate everyone.\n\nI didn&#x27;t want to just pick and choose my best friends (it&#x27;s only November and we are freshmen so I don&#x27;t have a close group yet) so I figured I would send invites based on who likes Rick and Morty the most.\n\nI put together three quizzes. One for guys (hard- because I know more males are interested in attending and I want it to be harder for them to gain entry just because of the gender ratio) one for girls (intermediate, to increase the number of girls) and one for girls I find attractive (easy, because I&#x27;m hoping this party could open me up to potential cute girls to hook up with or date.)\n\nShockingly, only a couple people have filled out the quiz and their write-in responses are too inappropriate for me to write here. NONE of the girls filled it out. Now nobody wants to go. So I sent out a group message saying that if nobody is willing to fill out the quiz I am more than happy to have this party just myself and my roommate. Someone responded &quot;good, wrong, nobody wants to come.&quot;\n\nTo be clear, everyone wanted to come prior to the sending of the quizzes AND...it&#x27;s a free party. I&#x27;m allowed to bar entry however I want...right? I mean nobody is entitled to my TV.<\/div><\/div><p><strong>Do you think the writer was in the wrong?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"v_1224","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for barring entry to my party with a quiz? I am hosting a R","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely not in the wrong"},"2":{"Display":"Probably not in the wrong"},"3":{"Display":"Unsure"},"4":{"Display":"Probably in the wrong"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely in the wrong"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID195","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID196","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_v_1224","QuestionID":"QID196","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID197","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for barring entry to my party with a quiz? I am hosting a R","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for barring entry to my party with a quiz? I am hosting a Rick and Morty screening party in my dorm room next week. I am one of the only people in the dorm with a good TV so a lot of people want to come but the room can&#x27;t accommodate everyone.\n\nI didn&#x27;t want to just pick and choose my best friends (it&#x27;s only November and we are freshmen so I don&#x27;t have a close group yet) so I figured I would send invites based on who likes Rick and Morty the most.\n\nI put together three quizzes. One for guys (hard- because I know more males are interested in attending and I want it to be harder for them to gain entry just because of the gender ratio) one for girls (intermediate, to increase the number of girls) and one for girls I find attractive (easy, because I&#x27;m hoping this party could open me up to potential cute girls to hook up with or date.)\n\nShockingly, only a couple people have filled out the quiz and their write-in responses are too inappropriate for me to write here. NONE of the girls filled it out. Now nobody wants to go. So I sent out a group message saying that if nobody is willing to fill out the quiz I am more than happy to have this party just myself and my roommate. Someone responded &quot;good, wrong, nobody wants to come.&quot;\n\nTo be clear, everyone wanted to come prior to the sending of the quizzes AND...it&#x27;s a free party. I&#x27;m allowed to bar entry however I want...right? I mean nobody is entitled to my TV.<\/div><\/div><p><em>You can re-read the situation above while evaluating the responses.<\/em><\/p><p>Here are two responses to the writer.<\/p><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;align-items:start\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response A<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option A}<\/div><\/div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response B<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option B}<\/div><\/div><\/div><p><strong>Overall, how good is each response?<\/strong><\/p><p>Rate each response:<\/p><p><strong>Response A<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gA_1224","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for barring entry to my party with a quiz? I am hosting a R","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID197","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID198","SecondaryAttribute":"Response B","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Response B<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gB_1224","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Response B","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID198","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID199","SecondaryAttribute":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"l_1224","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely Response A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably Response A"},"3":{"Display":"About equally likely to listen to both"},"4":{"Display":"Probably Response B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely Response B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID199","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID2","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for telling our 6 year old her dog \"de-aged\" rather than di","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for telling our 6 year old her dog &quot;de-aged&quot; rather than died? Our daughter has little concept of death. She knows what it is but has never experienced it. That is until our family dog passed at 12 years old, a little Cairn runt. She wasn&#x27;t sick, or in pain or injured, it was just her time I suppose. She passed in her sleep, laying in front of our fridge.\n\nWe decided to get another puppy right away, my husband organized it in under 24 hours. He came home with a little Cairn puppy, only 10 weeks old. Same color and everything. We surprised our daughter but made it out as if we were also surprised. We explained her dog de-aged back to a puppy. We even decided to name the dog the same name. Our daughter bought it and after two weeks hasn&#x27;t questioned anything.\n\nMy parents think we&#x27;re setting her up for a very difficult conversation when she gets older and a skewed sense of death. On the other hand, we don&#x27;t know how to approach this topic because she truly loved the dog to no end. We don&#x27;t see what we&#x27;ve done as negative, but we&#x27;ll leave this for others to judge.<\/div><\/div><p><em>You can re-read the situation above while evaluating the responses.<\/em><\/p><p>Here are two responses to the writer.<\/p><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;align-items:start\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response A<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option A}<\/div><\/div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response B<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option B}<\/div><\/div><\/div><p><strong>Overall, how good is each response?<\/strong><\/p><p>Rate each response:<\/p><p><strong>Response A<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gA_921","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for telling our 6 year old her dog \"de-aged\" rather than di","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID2","PrivateData":false,"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"NextChoiceId":8,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID20","SecondaryAttribute":"Study Instructions This study takes about 8\u201312 minutes. You will read 5 situations in which someo.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<h2>Study Instructions<\/h2><p>This study takes about 8\u201312 minutes.<\/p><p><br><\/p><p>You will read <strong>5 situations<\/strong> in which someone describes an interpersonal disagreement and asks for moral advice.<\/p><p>For each situation:<\/p><ol><li>First, say whether you think the writer was in the wrong.<\/li><li>On the next page, you will see the situation again, read two responses, and rate those responses.<\/li><\/ol><p><br><\/p><p>Please confirm you are not a robot.<\/p><p><br><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"intro_captcha","QuestionType":"Captcha","Selector":"V2","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","Align":"left","Theme":"light"},"QuestionDescription":"Study Instructions This study takes about 8\u201312 minutes. You will read 5 situations in which someo...","GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID20","PrivateData":false,"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"NextChoiceId":1,"NextAnswerId":1}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID200","SecondaryAttribute":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would you rather get advice from?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"a_1224","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely commenter A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably commenter A"},"3":{"Display":"No preference"},"4":{"Display":"Probably commenter B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely commenter B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID200","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID201","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_r_1224","QuestionID":"QID201","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID202","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Would I be wrong if I Suggest Transfering My Coworker? Would I be wron","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Would I be wrong if I Suggest Transfering My Coworker? Would I be wrong if I Suggest Transfering My CoWorker?\n\nBack Story:\n\nOur team&#x27;s (10 people) boss is away for 3 weeks. I&#x27;m in charge of our team while she&#x27;s gone. One of my team members named Adam is autistic or something.\n\nSince our boss left hes been completely mute. Refuses to say a word. I&#x27;ve been here 6 months and Adam 3ish years.\n\nI said something to my coworkers and they&#x27;re like &quot;ya, sometimes he gets that way when he&#x27;s stressed&quot; and shrugged it off. One even made a joke about it saying he will have to talk more to fill the quietness.\n\nHow do they not see the issue here? He can&#x27;t answer phones when a customer calls. He&#x27;s wasting time writing things down when he needs to speak to someone. If a customer needs help he takes them to the item instead of just telling them the area.\n\nI&#x27;ve been making him stock the shelves and tidy them during anyone&#x27;s scheduled time to do it since we have to answer the phone for him.\n\nNo customers have complained, but I think they&#x27;re just being nice because he&#x27;s special needs. If I was a customer, I wouldn&#x27;t be happy.\n\nWould I be wrong if I say something to our Boss when she gets back.\n\nI mean I&#x27;m all for handicapped people working and all but he obviously can&#x27;t handle the job if he goes mute. I want to say something to get the boss to transfer him elsewhere or &#x27;suggest&#x27; he finds another job.\n\nJust because he&#x27;s stubborn doesnt mean he should get special treatment.<\/div><\/div><p><strong>Do you think the writer was in the wrong?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"v_3911","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Would I be wrong if I Suggest Transfering My Coworker? Would I be wron","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely not in the wrong"},"2":{"Display":"Probably not in the wrong"},"3":{"Display":"Unsure"},"4":{"Display":"Probably in the wrong"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely in the wrong"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID202","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID203","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_v_3911","QuestionID":"QID203","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID204","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Would I be wrong if I Suggest Transfering My Coworker? Would I be wron","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Would I be wrong if I Suggest Transfering My Coworker? Would I be wrong if I Suggest Transfering My CoWorker?\n\nBack Story:\n\nOur team&#x27;s (10 people) boss is away for 3 weeks. I&#x27;m in charge of our team while she&#x27;s gone. One of my team members named Adam is autistic or something.\n\nSince our boss left hes been completely mute. Refuses to say a word. I&#x27;ve been here 6 months and Adam 3ish years.\n\nI said something to my coworkers and they&#x27;re like &quot;ya, sometimes he gets that way when he&#x27;s stressed&quot; and shrugged it off. One even made a joke about it saying he will have to talk more to fill the quietness.\n\nHow do they not see the issue here? He can&#x27;t answer phones when a customer calls. He&#x27;s wasting time writing things down when he needs to speak to someone. If a customer needs help he takes them to the item instead of just telling them the area.\n\nI&#x27;ve been making him stock the shelves and tidy them during anyone&#x27;s scheduled time to do it since we have to answer the phone for him.\n\nNo customers have complained, but I think they&#x27;re just being nice because he&#x27;s special needs. If I was a customer, I wouldn&#x27;t be happy.\n\nWould I be wrong if I say something to our Boss when she gets back.\n\nI mean I&#x27;m all for handicapped people working and all but he obviously can&#x27;t handle the job if he goes mute. I want to say something to get the boss to transfer him elsewhere or &#x27;suggest&#x27; he finds another job.\n\nJust because he&#x27;s stubborn doesnt mean he should get special treatment.<\/div><\/div><p><em>You can re-read the situation above while evaluating the responses.<\/em><\/p><p>Here are two responses to the writer.<\/p><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;align-items:start\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response A<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option A}<\/div><\/div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response B<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option B}<\/div><\/div><\/div><p><strong>Overall, how good is each response?<\/strong><\/p><p>Rate each response:<\/p><p><strong>Response A<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gA_3911","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Would I be wrong if I Suggest Transfering My Coworker? Would I be wron","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID204","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID205","SecondaryAttribute":"Response B","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Response B<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gB_3911","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Response B","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID205","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID206","SecondaryAttribute":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"l_3911","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely Response A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably Response A"},"3":{"Display":"About equally likely to listen to both"},"4":{"Display":"Probably Response B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely Response B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID206","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID207","SecondaryAttribute":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would you rather get advice from?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"a_3911","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely commenter A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably commenter A"},"3":{"Display":"No preference"},"4":{"Display":"Probably commenter B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely commenter B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID207","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID208","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_r_3911","QuestionID":"QID208","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID209","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for wanting some physical affection I (f) am in a long dist","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for wanting some physical affection I (f) am in a long distance relationship with another girl. I&#x27;m on the west coast (USA) and she&#x27;s on the east coast (USA). I love her more than I have ever loved anyone else. We&#x27;re still in the honeymoon stage 6 months into our relationship. Recently I&#x27;ve been talking with guy friend of mine who goes to my school. He&#x27;s been confused about his sexuality for a while and we talk about that a lot. I would just like to clarify that I am a lesbian meaning I have NO feelings towards this guy or any guy what-so-ever. The last time we hung out, we just cuddled and watched TV. It was really nice to just have some physical affection, no strings attached. As I was leaving he said &quot;I love you!&quot;, which isn&#x27;t odd we say that to each other all the time, but he just had a more serious tone in his voice. After talking with him I found out he had a crush on me. I&#x27;m loyal to my girlfriend and I don&#x27;t like him at all, but I crave physical affection. No kissing, just some cuddling while watching a movie or TV. He follows me on my social media so he must know I have a girlfriend, cause I post about her all the time. She doesn&#x27;t know that I have spent time with this guy, she gets pretty jealous at even the slightest of contact with anyone else. Am I wrong for 1. not telling my girlfriend and 2. ignoring this boys crush on me and using him as a cuddle partner?<\/div><\/div><p><strong>Do you think the writer was in the wrong?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"v_1414","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for wanting some physical affection I (f) am in a long dist","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely not in the wrong"},"2":{"Display":"Probably not in the wrong"},"3":{"Display":"Unsure"},"4":{"Display":"Probably in the wrong"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely in the wrong"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID209","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID21","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for ignoring reserved parking signs at super markets? So th","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for ignoring reserved parking signs at super markets? So this one is pretty stupid I apologize. I work in food and bev distribution which means I visit several grocery stores daily. I began to get annoyed when I noticed they all seem to have reserved parking for just about everybody. Shop from home customers only, veterans only, expectant mothers only, mothers with small children, etc. Now with the exception of handicap parking, I decided these were all nonsense and cheap pr stunts, and thus started parking where ever I found a spot. These spots are nearly always open and noone seems to miss them.\n\nA woman finally called me out for parking in the pregnant woman spot to which I said &quot;ok&quot; and basically ignored her. Now I know I&#x27;m in the wrong here I guess, but am I correct in it not being a big deal and a nonsense pr thing, or am I really just A total d***?<\/div><\/div><p><strong>Do you think the writer was in the wrong?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"v_3488","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for ignoring reserved parking signs at super markets? So th","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely not in the wrong"},"2":{"Display":"Probably not in the wrong"},"3":{"Display":"Unsure"},"4":{"Display":"Probably in the wrong"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely in the wrong"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID21","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID210","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_v_1414","QuestionID":"QID210","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID211","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for wanting some physical affection I (f) am in a long dist","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for wanting some physical affection I (f) am in a long distance relationship with another girl. I&#x27;m on the west coast (USA) and she&#x27;s on the east coast (USA). I love her more than I have ever loved anyone else. We&#x27;re still in the honeymoon stage 6 months into our relationship. Recently I&#x27;ve been talking with guy friend of mine who goes to my school. He&#x27;s been confused about his sexuality for a while and we talk about that a lot. I would just like to clarify that I am a lesbian meaning I have NO feelings towards this guy or any guy what-so-ever. The last time we hung out, we just cuddled and watched TV. It was really nice to just have some physical affection, no strings attached. As I was leaving he said &quot;I love you!&quot;, which isn&#x27;t odd we say that to each other all the time, but he just had a more serious tone in his voice. After talking with him I found out he had a crush on me. I&#x27;m loyal to my girlfriend and I don&#x27;t like him at all, but I crave physical affection. No kissing, just some cuddling while watching a movie or TV. He follows me on my social media so he must know I have a girlfriend, cause I post about her all the time. She doesn&#x27;t know that I have spent time with this guy, she gets pretty jealous at even the slightest of contact with anyone else. Am I wrong for 1. not telling my girlfriend and 2. ignoring this boys crush on me and using him as a cuddle partner?<\/div><\/div><p><em>You can re-read the situation above while evaluating the responses.<\/em><\/p><p>Here are two responses to the writer.<\/p><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;align-items:start\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response A<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option A}<\/div><\/div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response B<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option B}<\/div><\/div><\/div><p><strong>Overall, how good is each response?<\/strong><\/p><p>Rate each response:<\/p><p><strong>Response A<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gA_1414","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for wanting some physical affection I (f) am in a long dist","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID211","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID212","SecondaryAttribute":"Response B","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Response B<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gB_1414","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Response B","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID212","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID213","SecondaryAttribute":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"l_1414","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely Response A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably Response A"},"3":{"Display":"About equally likely to listen to both"},"4":{"Display":"Probably Response B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely Response B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID213","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID214","SecondaryAttribute":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would you rather get advice from?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"a_1414","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely commenter A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably commenter A"},"3":{"Display":"No preference"},"4":{"Display":"Probably commenter B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely commenter B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID214","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID215","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_r_1414","QuestionID":"QID215","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID216","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for telling my gf off Sorry for bad english! This happened ","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for telling my gf off Sorry for bad english!\n\nThis happened quite a while ago but i&#x27;ve always wondered if i was an.\n\nI knew this girl who was a complete cunt. I can&#x27;t tell you enough how much of a cunt she was. I talked about her a lot with my gf, about how horrible she was, about the death threats she&#x27;d give.\n\nMy gf told me after a while of complaining about her that she wanted to be her friend since everyone hated her. I told her &#x27;please don&#x27;t, you don&#x27;t know what kind of things she has said&#x27; but she ignored me.\n\nThe awful girl was super nice around my gf, all the time. It was really weird. After about two weeks of being forced to be around the awful girl i had enough and didn&#x27;t accept mt gfs invitations if i knew she&#x27;d be there.\n\nThat didn&#x27;t work. I&#x27;m ashamed to admit i became really jealous and tried to show my gf what a lair that girl was. She had an excuse for everything on her behalf.\n\nI told my gf that i didn&#x27;t want her to be friends with that girl. She (understandably) told me that I couldn&#x27;t decide her friends. She hung around that girl until she moved.\n\nWe broke up shortly after.\n\nAnyway, was I in the wrong? I know it happened like 7 months ago but i still wonder.<\/div><\/div><p><strong>Do you think the writer was in the wrong?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"v_3064","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for telling my gf off Sorry for bad english! This happened ","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely not in the wrong"},"2":{"Display":"Probably not in the wrong"},"3":{"Display":"Unsure"},"4":{"Display":"Probably in the wrong"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely in the wrong"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID216","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID217","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_v_3064","QuestionID":"QID217","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID218","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for telling my gf off Sorry for bad english! This happened ","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for telling my gf off Sorry for bad english!\n\nThis happened quite a while ago but i&#x27;ve always wondered if i was an.\n\nI knew this girl who was a complete cunt. I can&#x27;t tell you enough how much of a cunt she was. I talked about her a lot with my gf, about how horrible she was, about the death threats she&#x27;d give.\n\nMy gf told me after a while of complaining about her that she wanted to be her friend since everyone hated her. I told her &#x27;please don&#x27;t, you don&#x27;t know what kind of things she has said&#x27; but she ignored me.\n\nThe awful girl was super nice around my gf, all the time. It was really weird. After about two weeks of being forced to be around the awful girl i had enough and didn&#x27;t accept mt gfs invitations if i knew she&#x27;d be there.\n\nThat didn&#x27;t work. I&#x27;m ashamed to admit i became really jealous and tried to show my gf what a lair that girl was. She had an excuse for everything on her behalf.\n\nI told my gf that i didn&#x27;t want her to be friends with that girl. She (understandably) told me that I couldn&#x27;t decide her friends. She hung around that girl until she moved.\n\nWe broke up shortly after.\n\nAnyway, was I in the wrong? I know it happened like 7 months ago but i still wonder.<\/div><\/div><p><em>You can re-read the situation above while evaluating the responses.<\/em><\/p><p>Here are two responses to the writer.<\/p><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;align-items:start\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response A<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option A}<\/div><\/div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response B<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option B}<\/div><\/div><\/div><p><strong>Overall, how good is each response?<\/strong><\/p><p>Rate each response:<\/p><p><strong>Response A<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gA_3064","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for telling my gf off Sorry for bad english! This happened ","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID218","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID219","SecondaryAttribute":"Response B","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Response B<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gB_3064","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Response B","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID219","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID22","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for ignoring reserved parking signs at super markets? So th","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for ignoring reserved parking signs at super markets? So this one is pretty stupid I apologize. I work in food and bev distribution which means I visit several grocery stores daily. I began to get annoyed when I noticed they all seem to have reserved parking for just about everybody. Shop from home customers only, veterans only, expectant mothers only, mothers with small children, etc. Now with the exception of handicap parking, I decided these were all nonsense and cheap pr stunts, and thus started parking where ever I found a spot. These spots are nearly always open and noone seems to miss them.\n\nA woman finally called me out for parking in the pregnant woman spot to which I said &quot;ok&quot; and basically ignored her. Now I know I&#x27;m in the wrong here I guess, but am I correct in it not being a big deal and a nonsense pr thing, or am I really just A total d***?<\/div><\/div><p><em>You can re-read the situation above while evaluating the responses.<\/em><\/p><p>Here are two responses to the writer.<\/p><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;align-items:start\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response A<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option A}<\/div><\/div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response B<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option B}<\/div><\/div><\/div><p><strong>Overall, how good is each response?<\/strong><\/p><p>Rate each response:<\/p><p><strong>Response A<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gA_3488","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for ignoring reserved parking signs at super markets? So th","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID22","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID220","SecondaryAttribute":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"l_3064","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely Response A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably Response A"},"3":{"Display":"About equally likely to listen to both"},"4":{"Display":"Probably Response B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely Response B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID220","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID221","SecondaryAttribute":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would you rather get advice from?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"a_3064","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely commenter A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably commenter A"},"3":{"Display":"No preference"},"4":{"Display":"Probably commenter B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely commenter B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID221","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID222","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_r_3064","QuestionID":"QID222","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID223","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for telling my ex \"why would you care\"? For context, we are","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for telling my ex &quot;why would you care&quot;? For context, we are still going to the same school and he still sits next to me in a lot of subjects. He broke up with me a month ago pretty much unexpected. Today I finally made up my mind and asked him a few questions. I asked him if he&#x27;d still care about me which he said no to or at least something like that. (I think, I slept very little and am horrible at recalling conversations). Then I asked him if he missed me which he also said no to. I told him &quot;I miss you quite a lot, shakes head but why would you care.&quot;\nHe then got angry and told me thati was incredibly manipulative. I meant it in a genuine way, mostly wanting to show the redundancy of my comment, which is also the reason why I shook my head. Basically over my own stupidity. I don&#x27;t think it&#x27;s something negative that he doesn&#x27;t care anymore and didn&#x27;t mean to blame him in any way. Good for him that he could just move on. Am I wrong for\n\nTL:DR I told my ex I missed him and then rhetorically asked why he would care. Didn&#x27;t mean it in a mean way though.<\/div><\/div><p><strong>Do you think the writer was in the wrong?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"v_453","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for telling my ex \"why would you care\"? For context, we are","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely not in the wrong"},"2":{"Display":"Probably not in the wrong"},"3":{"Display":"Unsure"},"4":{"Display":"Probably in the wrong"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely in the wrong"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID223","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID224","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_v_453","QuestionID":"QID224","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID225","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for telling my ex \"why would you care\"? For context, we are","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for telling my ex &quot;why would you care&quot;? For context, we are still going to the same school and he still sits next to me in a lot of subjects. He broke up with me a month ago pretty much unexpected. Today I finally made up my mind and asked him a few questions. I asked him if he&#x27;d still care about me which he said no to or at least something like that. (I think, I slept very little and am horrible at recalling conversations). Then I asked him if he missed me which he also said no to. I told him &quot;I miss you quite a lot, shakes head but why would you care.&quot;\nHe then got angry and told me thati was incredibly manipulative. I meant it in a genuine way, mostly wanting to show the redundancy of my comment, which is also the reason why I shook my head. Basically over my own stupidity. I don&#x27;t think it&#x27;s something negative that he doesn&#x27;t care anymore and didn&#x27;t mean to blame him in any way. Good for him that he could just move on. Am I wrong for\n\nTL:DR I told my ex I missed him and then rhetorically asked why he would care. Didn&#x27;t mean it in a mean way though.<\/div><\/div><p><em>You can re-read the situation above while evaluating the responses.<\/em><\/p><p>Here are two responses to the writer.<\/p><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;align-items:start\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response A<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option A}<\/div><\/div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response B<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option B}<\/div><\/div><\/div><p><strong>Overall, how good is each response?<\/strong><\/p><p>Rate each response:<\/p><p><strong>Response A<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gA_453","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for telling my ex \"why would you care\"? For 