ually likely to listen to both"},"4":{"Display":"Probably Response B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely Response B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID227","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID228","SecondaryAttribute":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would you rather get advice from?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"a_453","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely commenter A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably commenter A"},"3":{"Display":"No preference"},"4":{"Display":"Probably commenter B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely commenter B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID228","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID229","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_r_453","QuestionID":"QID229","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID23","SecondaryAttribute":"Response B","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Response B<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gB_3488","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Response B","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID23","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID230","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for kicking my employee out of the office? I am an Office M","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for kicking my employee out of the office? I am an Office Manager at a tax firm. We had to work today, but very few people showed up (they took vacation). Our boss said we could leave as early as 2PM and all but one person took him up on his offer. His name is Eric and he is an older gay guy. I don&#x27;t think he has family or any friends and he spoke about breaking up with his boyfriend a couple of years ago. Nice guy, hard worker, quiet yet obviously lonely. I told Eric he should just leave and whatever work he had could wait until Monday (which is 100% true and he&#x27;s ahead on his work). He declined and made up excuse after excuse as to why he needed to stay.\n\nSometimes he comes in at 8AM and doesn&#x27;t leave until 7PM even though his work schedule is 8:30AM to 5:30PM. He doesn&#x27;t ask for OT. My boss started to grow concern about his working so late because he thinks he&#x27;s overworked and suggested that I take on some of Eric&#x27;s work. That&#x27;s not the case at ALL. He just doesn&#x27;t have a life outside of work. He&#x27;s one of those people. I know my boss would find out that he stayed late, AGAIN and on a semi-holiday, and that would result in my having to take on his work. I told Eric that I wasn&#x27;t trying to be rude and knew he was working, but he had to leave - boss&#x27;s orders. He made a comment how it felt weird leaving work while there was still light and didn&#x27;t know what to do. I told him to go feed some homeless people.<\/div><\/div><p><strong>Do you think the writer was in the wrong?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"v_461","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for kicking my employee out of the office? I am an Office M","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely not in the wrong"},"2":{"Display":"Probably not in the wrong"},"3":{"Display":"Unsure"},"4":{"Display":"Probably in the wrong"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely in the wrong"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID230","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID231","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_v_461","QuestionID":"QID231","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"V