2412","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely Response A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably Response A"},"3":{"Display":"About equally likely to listen to both"},"4":{"Display":"Probably Response B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely Response B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID332","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID333","SecondaryAttribute":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would you rather get advice from?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"a_2412","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely commenter A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably commenter A"},"3":{"Display":"No preference"},"4":{"Display":"Probably commenter B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely commenter B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID333","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID334","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_r_2412","QuestionID":"QID334","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID335","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Would I be wrong if I left my GF home alone after she got a kidney sto","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Would I be wrong if I left my GF home alone after she got a kidney stone removed, to go to a party? Backstory: Yesterday my girlfriend was released from the hospital after being there for two days getting a kidney stone removed and recovering. We are supposed to go to a party tonight, but she is on pain killers so drinking is a no go. She does not want to attend and instead has requested me to stay home and take care of her.\nI want to attend as I rarely get to see this group of friends or go out for that matter. She is given the flexibility to go out when she likes and does so multiple times a month. Would I be wrong if I go to this party and leave her at home?<\/div><\/div><p><strong>Do you think the writer was in the wrong?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"v_1874","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Would I be wrong if I left my GF home alone after she got a kidney sto","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely not in the wrong"},