":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID51","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID510","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for eating my dad's last slice of pizza So my parents and I","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for eating my dad&#x27;s last slice of pizza So my parents and I got dinner because my dad didn&#x27;t feel like cooking so we all decided on Italian. My mom got chicken parm and my dad and I got pizza. We got half meat lovers and half cheese. My dad made it half cheese because he didn&#x27;t feel like having meat lovers. So we are eating and I grab my second helping and without thinking eat my dad&#x27;s last slice of cheese. When he finds this out he is furious and proceeds to angrily eat meat lover, throw a hissy fit, and call me a d***. After that he angrily goes upstairs even when my mother offered him numerous options such as pick the meat off, also mind you my dad is 49 years old in my mind this means he shouldn&#x27;t be acting like he&#x27;s 5. So then my mother proceeds to scold me calling me selfish and stuff and saying how I should see his point of view and apologize. am I wrong?<\/div><\/div><p><strong>Do you think the writer was in the wrong?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"v_3211","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for eating my dad's last slice of pizza So my parents and I","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely not in the wrong"},"2":{"Display":"Probably not in the wrong"},"3":{"Display":"Unsure"},"4":{"