 had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would you rather get advice from?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"a_3211","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely commenter A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably commenter A"},"3":{"Display":"No preference"},"4":{"Display":"Probably commenter B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely commenter B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID515","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID516","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_r_3211","QuestionID":"QID516","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID517","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for getting angry at my classmates for disrespecting our sp","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for getting angry at my classmates for disrespecting our specimens? I&#x27;m at university studying environmental science. Today whilst in a Laboratory class we had small worm specimens (no nervous system, the length of a fingernail). We were told to carefully move the specimens to the middle of our dish and create a current with a pipette. I was doing this when I look over a couple of seats next to me to see two girls being very rough and disrespectful to the dish\/specimen. I get up to see what they are doing (it&#x27;s pretty common to just have a snoop at what everyone else is doing). They are a bit rude when I approached them, being quite cold. So I walk away back to my table as they continue to abuse the worm (I know they don&#x27;t have a nervous system but they were being pretty disrespectful). So me being the loud mouth and stupid person that I am (also a bit angry from their cold reaction towards me) I called them &quot;retards who need to calm down and have more respect&quot; to my friends. Of course they heard me because I&#x27;m a loud mouth. I then see one of the girls look quite upset and they both kind of quiet down.\n\nI know it was completely wrong to call them &#x27;retards&#x27; because that is just not okay to use. But was I wrong in thinking that they were being disrespectful? I in no way thought they were harming the worm because these guys can be chopped up into 50 pieces and regenerate. But I believe (especially studying environmental science) you should have some respect for the life around you and for what we are doing and not take advantage.<\/div><\/div><p><strong>Do you think the writer was in the wrong?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"v_3150","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for getting angry at my classmates for disrespecting our sp","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely not in the wrong"},"2":{"Display":"Probably not in the wrong"},"3":{"Display":"Unsure"},"4":{"Display":"Probably in the wrong"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely in the wrong"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID517","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID518","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_v_3150","QuestionID":"QID518","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID519","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for getting angry at my classmates for disrespecting our sp","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for getting angry at my classmates for disrespecting our specimens? I&#x27;m at university studying environmental science. Today whilst in a Laboratory class we had small worm specimens (no nervous system, the length of a fingernail). We were told to carefully move the specimens to the middle of our dish and create a current with a pipette. I was doing this when I look over a couple of seats next to me to see two girls being very rough and disrespectful to the dish\/specimen. I get up to see what they are doing (it&#x27;s pretty common to just have a snoop at what everyone else is doing). They are a bit rude when I approached them, being quite cold. So I walk away back to my table as they continue to abuse the worm (I know they don&#x27;t have a nervous system but they were being pretty disrespectful). So me being the loud mouth and stupid person that I am (also a bit angry from their cold reaction towards me) I called them &quot;retards who need to calm down and have more respect&quot; to my friends. Of course they heard me because I&#x27;m a loud mouth. I then see one of the girls look quite upset and they both kind of quiet down.\n\nI know it was completely wrong to call them &#x27;retards&#x27; because that is just not okay to use. But was I wrong in thinking that they were being disrespectful? I in no way thought they were harming the worm because these guys can be chopped up into 50 pieces and regenerate. But I believe (especially studying environmental science) you should have some respect for the life around you and for what we are doing and not take advantage.<\/div><\/div><p><em>You can re-read the situation above while evaluating the responses.<\/em><\/p><p>Here are two responses to the writer.<\/p><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;align-items:start\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response A<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option A}<\/div><\/div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response B<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;backg