ommenters would y","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would you rather get advice from?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"a_602","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely commenter A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably commenter A"},"3":{"Display":"No preference"},"4":{"Display":"Probably commenter B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely commenter B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID550","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID551","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_r_602","QuestionID":"QID551","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID552","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Would I be wrong if I asked my sister not to give her baby the same na","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Would I be wrong if I asked my sister not to give her baby the same name as my husband&#x27;s dead brother So my husband had a brother but, sadly, he passed away at the age of 8. My husband was 7. He had leukemia. His parents had another baby a year after he died and they gave that baby the same name. They also have the same birthday. Anyway, his younger brother was sick as a baby and they were advised to change the name because it&#x27;s a baby omen. His younger brother has a different name now. So my sister is due in May and my husband&#x27;s dead brother&#x27;s name is on the list of names. I don&#x27;t want my future nephew to have a name with this history. My sister knows the whole story about my husband&#x27;s brothers and the name.\n\nSo Would I be wrong if I asked her to remove the name from her list of names? Prepared to be in the wrong because it&#x27;s their kid and they can name it whatever they want<\/div><\/div><p><strong>Do you think the writer was in the wrong?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"v_2516","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Would I be wrong if I asked my sister not to give her baby the same na","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely not in the wrong"},"2":{"Display":"Probably not in the wrong"},"3":{"Display":"Unsure"},"4":{"Display":"Probably in the wrong"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely in the wrong"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID552","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID553","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_v_2516","QuestionID":"QID553","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID554","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Would I be wrong if I asked my sister not to give her baby the same na","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Would I be wrong if I asked my sister not to give her baby the same name as my husband&#x27;s dead brother So my husband had a brother but, sadly, he passed away at the age of 8. My husband was 7. He had leukemia. His parents had another baby a year after he died and they gave that baby the same name. They also have the same birthday. Anyway, his younger brother was sick as a baby and they were advised to change the name because it&#x27;s a baby omen. His younger brother has a different name now. So my sister is due in May and my husband&#x27;s dead brother&#x27;s name is on the list of names. I don&#x27;t want my future nephew to have a name with this history. My sister knows the whole story about my husband&#x27;s brothers and the name.\n\nSo Would I be wrong if I asked her to remove the name from her list of names? Prepared to be in the wrong because it&#x27;s their kid and they can name it whatever they want<\/div><\/div><p><em>You can re-read the situation above while evaluating the responses.<\/em><\/p><p>Here are two responses to the writer.<\/p><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;align-items:start\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response A<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option A}<\/div><\/div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response B<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option B}<\/div><\/div><\/div><p><strong>Overall, how good is each response?<\/strong><\/p><p>Rate each response:<\/p><p><strong>Response A<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gA_2516","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Would I be wrong if I asked my sister not to give her baby the same na","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID554","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID555","SecondaryAttribute":"Response B","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Response B<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gB_2516","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Response B","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Very bad"},"2":{"Display":"Bad"},"3":{"Display":"Somewhat bad"},"4":{"Display":"Neither good nor bad"},"5":{"Display":"Somewhat good"},"6":{"Display":"Good"},"7":{"Display":"Very good"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5","6","7"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID555","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID556","SecondaryAttribute":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"l_2516","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely Response A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably Response A"},"3":{"Display":"About equally likely to listen to both"},"4":{"Display":"Probably Response B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely Response B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID556","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID557","SecondaryAttribute":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would you rather get advice from?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"a_2516","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"If you had a personal problem of your own, which of these two commenters would y","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely commenter A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably commenter A"},"3":{"Display":"No preference"},"4":{"Display":"Probably commenter B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely commenter B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID557","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID558","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_r_2516","QuestionID":"QID558","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID559","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for kicking my sister out of my wedding during the receptio","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for kicking my sister out of my wedding during the reception? Throwaway for obvious reasons.\n\nI got married last Saturday. Hooray for me! My sister was my maid of honor. During her speech, she brought up her depression and how my husband supported her through it and how &quot;in that moment, I knew he was the one for throwaway...&quot; (so cliche!). I thought her speech was really selfish. I think it&#x27;s super inappropriate to bring up a mental illness during a wedding speech. Not only that, but the entire speech was about her. At MY wedding. 90% of the guests congratulated her afterwards and talked about how &quot;strong&quot; she was. Nobody was paying attention to me, at my own wedding! Sorry if I sound selfish, but IMO there is a time and a place for this sort of thing. So after the guests all greeted her, I asked her to leave and told her she was being disruptive and selfish. She was really upset but just left without arguing. My parents agree with me. but my husband and all of my close friends think I was way too harsh. Am I wrong?<\/div><\/div><p><strong>Do you think the writer was in the wrong?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"v_1738","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for kicking my sister out of my wedding during the receptio","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely not in the wrong"},"2":{"Display":"Probably not in the wrong"},"3":{"Display":"Unsure"},"4":{"Display":"Probably in the wrong"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely in the wrong"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID559","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID56","SecondaryAttribute":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p><strong>Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"l_787","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Which response do you think the writer would be more likely to listen to?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Definitely Response A"},"2":{"Display":"Probably Response A"},"3":{"Display":"About equally likely to listen to both"},"4":{"Display":"Probably Response B"},"5":{"Display":"Definitely Response B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"QuestionID":"QID56","PrivateData":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID560","SecondaryAttribute":"Timing","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Timing","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"t_v_1738","QuestionID":"QID560","QuestionType":"Timing","Selector":"PageTimer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":true},"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionDescription":"Timing","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"First Click"},"2":{"Display":"Last Click"},"3":{"Display":"Page Submit"},"4":{"Display":"Click Count"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3","4"],"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_ekvji0xKlx9Ac7Q","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID561","SecondaryAttribute":"Situation Am I wrong for kicking my sister out of my wedding during the receptio","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Situation<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">Am I wrong for kicking my sister out of my wedding during the reception? Throwaway for obvious reasons.\n\nI got married last Saturday. Hooray for me! My sister was my maid of honor. During her speech, she brought up her depression and how my husband supported her through it and how &quot;in that moment, I knew he was the one for throwaway...&quot; (so cliche!). I thought her speech was really selfish. I think it&#x27;s super inappropriate to bring up a mental illness during a wedding speech. Not only that, but the entire speech was about her. At MY wedding. 90% of the guests congratulated her afterwards and talked about how &quot;strong&quot; she was. Nobody was paying attention to me, at my own wedding! Sorry if I sound selfish, but IMO there is a time and a place for this sort of thing. So after the guests all greeted her, I asked her to leave and told her she was being disruptive and selfish. She was really upset but just left without arguing. My parents agree with me. but my husband and all of my close friends think I was way too harsh. Am I wrong?<\/div><\/div><p><em>You can re-read the situation above while evaluating the responses.<\/em><\/p><p>Here are two responses to the writer.<\/p><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:12px;align-items:start\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response A<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option A}<\/div><\/div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 4px 0;font-weight:600\">Response B<\/div><div style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:visible;height:auto;min-height:4em;background:#f7f6f3;border:1px solid #d9d6cf;padding:12px;line-height:1.45\">${e:\/\/Field\/Option B}<\/div><\/div><\/div><p><strong>Overall, how good is each response?<\/strong><\/p><p>Rate each response:<\/p><p><strong>Response A<\/strong><\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"gA_1738","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Situation Am I wrong for kicking my sister out of my wedding during the receptio"